        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0829" n="815" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg815"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Milledge, district attorney, to Mr. Hoar,
                        Attorney-General.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Macon, Georgia</hi></placeName>,
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1869-09-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >September</hi> 3, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">To Attorney-General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hoar</hi>:</p>
                <p>Large party of men, thoroughly armed, at Fort Gaines, Georgia, enlisted <pb
                        facs="0830" n="816" xml:id="pg816"/> for Cuban army. United States deputy
                    marshal finds it impossible to arrest, as the citizens are not sufficiently
                    strong; he telegraphs for troops to assist. General Terry replies that General
                    Halleck will not give the authority. What course shall I pursue? They will get
                    off on special boat to-morrow. Answer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN MILLEDGE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States District
                            Attorney.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
